notes:
27x27 -> 20x20, 11,913 -> 6,938 local ticks. Three changes:
1. Track the ring phase rather than restoring it. ROT2 is gone; the ring is left where ACCESS
   left it and the next round rotates (v'-1-v) mod 9 — five pops a round instead of nine, one
   fewer block. Phase rides in the scratch FIFO; "rq M L8 - M" turns last round's v into K = 8-v
   in B, where it survives three ri/sq pairs untouched, and "M L9 W %" is the whole modulus.
2. Overlap the pipe bands. Incoming at 7/5/11, outgoing at 3/1/13 keeps the round's rq/sq chatter
   in the middle: 69 glyphs in 9 rows of 11 columns. Ring ops pushed east free the east strip for
   the rotation loop, its exit corridor and ACCESS, none of which then costs a row.
3. Mirror the round — generated top-down and flipped, so entry lands bottom-left where OK's and
   INIT's returns arrive and exit lands top-right beside the rotation loop. Return corridor is
   one cell. INIT shares BAD's row since A is 0 throughout INIT.

Side 13 proved unreachable on cell count: aux is 85 cells minimum (I 9 + O 9 + two turnarounds 48
+ pipes 19) and the 69-glyph round needs an 11x9 outer at unreachable density — 184 > 169.
The 27x27 build (sudoku-validity_ring.man) is untouched and remains as a second solution.
